{"type":"plan","title":"The Mended Kite","logline":"A torn kite teaches a girl and her grandfather that love can stitch the wind back together.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Establishing view of Brighton seafront at windy autumn morning; Maya stands on the shingle beach, holding the string of her red kite which soars high above the pier railings.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[1,3,5]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close‑up on the kite as a sudden gust slams it into the iron railings; the red sail tears cleanly from corner to corner, fibers fluttering in the wind.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[1,3,6]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya runs along the shingle beach toward home, the broken kite hugged tightly to her chest, wind tugging at her raincoat.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[1,3,5]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"In the warm kitchen morning light, Grandfather sits at the wooden table, newspaper lowered, looking up with gentle curiosity as Maya enters.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[2,4]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Over-the-shoulder","description":"Over Grandfather's shoulder: the kite laid flat on the table, his hands threading a needle with white sailcloth thread, ready to stitch.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[2,3,4]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Extreme close‑up on the needle pulling thread through the torn sail; Grandfather points to each stitch, Maya watches intently.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[2,3,4]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Insert/detail","description":"Detail insert: Maya's small paintbrush adds a tiny gold star over the fresh seam; the star glints in the morning light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[3]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Afternoon light on the seafront; Maya and Grandfather walk side by side along the wet sand, the mended kite tucked under Grandfather's arm.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[1,3,5]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle looking up: Maya sprints into the strengthening wind, the kite surges higher than ever, its tail streaming over the rolling waves.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[1,3,5,6]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Two-shot","description":"Two‑shot of Maya and Grandfather on the sand; Maya hands the kite string to him, both laughing like children as the kite dances overhead.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[1,3]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Golden dusk bathes the beach; Maya and Grandfather stroll home along the sand, the mended kite resting on Maya's shoulder, its gold star catching the last light.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[1,3]}]}
